questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot service suffers from progressive memory growth and frequent `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space` under sustained load. A heap dump reveals millions of `byte[]` arrays retained inside thread pools. Inspecting the code reveals the following component:

java
@Service
public class DataExportService {
    private static final ThreadLocal<byte[]> PROCESSING_BUFFER = new ThreadLocal<>();

    @Async
    @Transactional(readOnly = true)
    public CompletableFuture<ExportResult> exportData(ExportRequest request) {
        byte[] buffer = new byte[5 * 1024 * 1024]; // 5MB allocation per task
        PROCESSING_BUFFER.set(buffer);

        ExportResult result = performProcessing(request);
        return CompletableFuture.completedFuture(result);
    }
}
